mcq:
Q: What is the quotient set for the equivalence relation of congruence modulo 3 on the set {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}?
  (A) {{0}, {1}, {2}, {3}, {4}, {5}}
  (B) {{0, 3}, {1, 4}, {2, 5}}
  (C) {{0, 1, 2}, {3, 4, 5}}
  (D) {{0}, {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}}
  answer: B  |  The quotient set for congruence modulo 3 on {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5} consists of the equivalence classes [0] = {0, 3}, [1] = {1, 4}, and [2] = {2, 5}.
